<title>GERMANY: Bonn's Stark says to make euro debt proposal soon.</title>
<headline>Bonn's Stark says to make euro debt proposal soon.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Juergen Stark, state secretary in the German finance ministry, said on Tuesday he would make a proposal on converting German debt into the euro by the summer break.</p>
<p>Stark said earlier at a Bundesbank news conference that he would recommend to German Finance Minister Theo Waigel that the country's debt be converted into euro in 1999.</p>
<p>The Bundesbank had called the news conference to announce the issuance of a new strippable 30-year bond.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
